        <qualifiedname>AGE::BufferLayout::BufferLayout</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para><ref refid="class_a_g_e_1_1_buffer_layout" kindref="compound">BufferLayout</ref> is a class that represents the layout of a buffer in memory. It provides methods for adding elements to the buffer and retrieving them by index. The buffer can hold any type of data, but it&apos;s typically used with primitive types like int, float, etc. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><ref refid="class_a_g_e_1_1_buffer_layout" kindref="compound">BufferLayout</ref> is a class that represents the layout of a buffer in memory.</para>
<para>This class provides methods for managing and manipulating the layout of a buffer in memory. It does not handle the actual data within the buffer, only its structure. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
